# TC-01 Canary Deploy Checklist

Workflow chain: WF-SILVER-FEATURE -> WF-SILVER-DEVOPS -> WF-SILVER-RELEASE.

## Preflight

- Confirm branch is `feature/tri-codex-tc-01-20260706t015239z-tc-01`.
- Run `npm test` from the repository root and confirm all waitlist, orders, health, and UI checks pass.
- Build local runtime with `docker compose build waitlist`.
- Start canary locally with `docker compose up waitlist`.
- Confirm `/health` returns HTTP 200 and `{ "status": "ok" }`.

## Canary

- Submit `POST /waitlist` with header `x-tenant-id: canary-a` and a canary email.
- Submit the same email under `x-tenant-id: canary-b` and confirm it is accepted independently.
- Repeat the first signup under `canary-a` and confirm the response status is `exists`.
- Call `GET /waitlist/stats` for both tenants and confirm totals remain isolated.
- Open `/` and submit through the landing page with the same tenant header flow handled by the tenant input.

## Abort Conditions

- Any 5xx from `/health`, `/waitlist`, or `/waitlist/stats`.
- Stats from one tenant include signups from another tenant.
- SQLite database file cannot be created under `WAITLIST_DB_PATH`.
- Duplicate POST increments tenant stats.

## Rollback

- Stop the canary container with `docker compose down`.
- Preserve `/data/waitlist.sqlite` for incident review if tenant isolation or duplicate handling fails.
- Revert the application image to the prior release and rerun `/health`.

